#!/usr/bin/python3
"""lsstcheck - cross-match a transient against LSST, TNS, and the Rubin schedule.

Resolves a TNS-style name, survey/internal name, LSST diaObjectId, or
sky position, then reports:

  * the LSST object identity (diaObjectId / LSST-*-DO name) and a
    clickable LASAIR link,
  * alternative names from the TNS public catalog,
  * the next scheduled Rubin pointing that covers the position, or
    an explicit note when the published schedule has none.

Examples:
    lsstcheck 2024lwa                  # TNS name
    lsstcheck AT2024lwa                # with prefix
    lsstcheck ZTF26abfwokm             # survey/internal name
    lsstcheck 170587106692825120       # LSST diaObjectId
    lsstcheck 338.196 -9.447           # RA Dec in decimal degrees
    lsstcheck "338.196,-9.447,60"      # ra,dec,radius in arcsec
    lsstcheck 13:32:47.04 -09:26:49.0   # sexagesimal
"""

